{"id":"hebridean-way","title":"Hebridean Way by bike","who":"Classic route · the Outer Hebrides, Scotland","when":"May to September","vehicle":"Bike, 6–8 days","kind":"bike","color":"#0891b2","summary":"297 km across ten islands, six causeways and two ferries from Vatersay to the Butt of Lewis: white beaches and turquoise water, Gaelic-speaking crofting townships, the mountains of Harris and the standing stones of Calanais. Headwinds are part of the deal, and so are ferry problems: in spring 2026 a third of CalMac's fleet was out of service. Keep spare days.","sources":[{"label":"CalMac: network update (March 2026)","url":"https://www.calmac.co.uk/en-gb/travel/latest-customer-updates/customer-update-network-update-march-2026/"},{"label":"Cycling UK: travellers' tales, Hebridean e-biking (2025)","url":"https://www.cyclinguk.org/cycle-magazine/travellers-tales-hebridean-e-biking"},{"label":"VisitScotland: Hebridean Way cycling route","url":"https://www.visitscotland.com/things-to-do/outdoor-activities/cycling/hebridean-way-cycling-route"}],"approximate":"Main stops; ferries between islands drawn as dashed lines.","km":303,"bbox":[-7.5434,56.9274,-6.2449,58.5156],"stops":[{"name":"Vatersay","place":"Vatersay","at":[56.9291,-7.5367],"text":"The southern start, past two white beaches.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Vatersay%2C_Bagh_Siar.jpg/500px-Vatersay%2C_Bagh_Siar.jpg","page":"Vatersay","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vatersay%2C_Bagh_Siar.jpg","credit":"Dougsim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Barra","place":"Castlebay, Barra","at":[57.0018,-7.4697],"text":"Kisimul castle in the bay; planes land on the beach here."},{"name":"Eriskay","place":"Eriskay","at":[57.0754,-7.2919],"text":"Ferry over the Sound of Barra; the \"Whisky Galore\" island.","by":"ferry","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Prince%E2%80%99s_Beach_%28The_Prince%E2%80%99s_Cockleshell_Strand%29_with_